{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And the eyes of Leah were tender</b> Three verses beginning with this phrase in the Masorah: here, and ועיני ישראל כבדו מזוקן, and ועיני רשעים תכלינה. Why were her eyes tender? Because she was afraid lest she be married to Esau. And similarly ועיני ישראל כבדו מזוקן — because he saw that Jeroboam and Ahab would descend from him. And this is the connection: ועיני לאה רכות and ועיני ישראל כבדו — on account of ועיני רשעים." "<b>Tender</b> Twice: ועיני לאה רכות, אם ידבר אליך רכות. Even so, he did not love her."], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Kitzur Baal HaTurim" "http://sefaria.org"] ["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:17:22.465694960Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}